WEBVTT

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:05.940
So hot...

00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:08.000
Melting...

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:09.470
Gonna die...

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:12.740
Is it seriously December right now?

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:15.860
They say we'll have a mild winter this year.

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:22.320
Calling temperatures above 30°C a 
"mild winter" is a bit of a stretch!

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:25.130
I mean, is it really even winter right now?

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:28.160
Why do we have to clean the pool in winter?!

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:30.810
It's a normal winter on the mainland.

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:33.650
You're doing this instead 
of supplementary lessons, right?

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:36.800
Because after arriving late 
and leaving early so often,

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:38.830
your attendance dropped too low.

00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:40.800
It's not like I was playing hooky for fun!

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:43.680
I mean, I only almost 
got killed a few times,

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:45.520
got stuck on a deserted island,

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:49.150
and got launched on a missile, that's all!

00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:53.970
And seriously, 
cleaning a pool alone in the blazing sun?

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:58.420
Natsuki-chan, there's got to be a limit 
to how much you can bully vampires!

00:00:59.770 --> 00:01:03.020
Don't feel so bad. 
Let's just get this done quickly.

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:09.060
I'll help you out.

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:12.480
Huh? Oh... Thanks, Himeragi.

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:14.090
Don't mention it.

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:18.930
It's my job to observe you, 
the Fourth Progenitor.

00:01:22.610 --> 00:01:24.120
D-Did you see?

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:24.700
Yep.

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:28.190
Senpai!

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:32.450
H-Hang on, Himeragi! 
That was purely accidental!

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:35.090
Besides, it was less like I saw it

00:01:35.090 --> 00:01:37.540
and more like you showed me...

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:43.780
Honestly... I see you're 
as indecent as ever, Senpai!

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:47.740
Whoa! That's a really high-pressure hose—

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:50.370
Sheesh.

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:54.300
Are you two really flirting again 
under the guise of pool cleaning?

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:56.960
We're not flirting!

00:01:56.960 --> 00:01:57.930
That's right!

00:01:58.160 --> 00:01:59.780
Yeah, sure.

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:01.460
Well, even though it's winter,

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:04.140
it's definitely the right weather 
for playing in the water.

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:07.840
So why stop at a dinky 
school pool like this?

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:13.470
Wouldn't you rather go check that out?

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:14.230
<b>Itogami Island's Newest
Fantasy Marine Resort</b>

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:15.090
What? You mean...

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:16.240
...that Blue Ely place?

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:18.810
Yeah. Since it's open 
on a provisional basis,

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:22.590
entry and lodging for two days 
and two nights is currently free!

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:25.740
We'll also invite Nagisa-chan, 
and Asagi said she's in, too.

00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:29.460
How 'bout it? Pretty sweet deal, right?

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:38.010
<i>The town was Itogami Island,</i>

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:44.800
<i>a manmade island constructed 
of carbon fiber, resin, metal, and magic,</i>

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:46.720
<i>sitting on the Pacific Ocean.</i>

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:52.970
<i>This town, designated a demon district 
for the protection of demon races,</i>

00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:54.460
<i>was home to a certain young man...</i>

00:02:56.580 --> 00:02:58.670
<i>The Fourth Progenitor.</i>

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:02.960
<i>The fourth of the Progenitors, 
who, by all rights, should not exist.</i>

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:07.010
<i>He would later build his own empire</i>

00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:10.330
<i>and reign over the whole 
world as its emperor.</i>

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:15.430
<i>His name was Akatsuki Kojou.</i>

00:04:56.340 --> 00:04:57.820
Can you keep running?

00:04:57.940 --> 00:04:58.790
Yeah!

00:04:58.790 --> 00:05:00.030
Don't let them get away!

00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:00.980
That way! After them!

00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:06.650
<i>Welcome to Blue Elysium.</i>

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:12.570
<i>This facility will open next year 
as Itogami Island's first true resort.</i>

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:14.550
<i>Our monitoring guests are invited to enjoy</i>

00:05:14.550 --> 00:05:17.210
<i>our magical beast park 
and many other attractions,</i>

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:21.860
<i>as well as nine types of pools, 
before they open to the public.</i>

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:23.420
Radaman Kitchen

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:26.130
Three orders of magical beast yakisoba,

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:28.400
a merman shake, and two harpy oolong teas.

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:30.320
That'll be 2,250 yen, please.

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:31.200
Kojou!

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:33.840
Got it! Three orders of magical 
beast yakisoba coming up!

00:05:34.030 --> 00:05:35.850
God, this grill's hot!

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:39.050
I'm gonna die! I'm gonna burn! 
I'm gonna turn to ash!

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:40.980
Order up!

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:42.980
Thank you very much!

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:42.980
You can have my pickled ginger.

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:48.740
Damn it, he tricked me.

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:51.890
This is nothing like what Yaze told us.

00:05:51.890 --> 00:05:54.450
Well, I figured <i>something</i> was up.

00:05:54.880 --> 00:05:57.400
When he brings up a sweet deal like that,

00:05:57.400 --> 00:05:59.410
there's always a catch to it somewhere.

00:05:59.550 --> 00:06:01.780
Open on a provisional basis, my ass.

00:06:01.780 --> 00:06:04.450
It's as crowded as it would be 
if it was open to the public.

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:05.850
Jeez...

00:06:12.410 --> 00:06:13.300
What?

00:06:13.820 --> 00:06:16.080
Nothing... never mind.

00:06:17.130 --> 00:06:22.080
Anyway, as long as we work, 
Nagisa and the other girls get to stay for free,

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:23.480
so I guess I can't complain.

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:26.740
They ended up missing 
out on their school trip,

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:29.380
so I hope this makes up for it a little.

00:06:30.810 --> 00:06:31.670
Excuse me.

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:33.190
Coming!

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:40.060
Wow, talk about huge!

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:42.080
This really is the world's biggest—

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:43.840
Is that a horse?!

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:45.940
A horse mermaid?!

00:06:45.940 --> 00:06:47.800
It's a hippocampus.

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:49.440
I guess it's a type of sea horse.

00:06:49.890 --> 00:06:51.840
Its eyes are so cute!

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:54.130
I wish I could feed it, too!

00:06:54.950 --> 00:06:56.720
What's wrong, Yukina-chan?

00:06:56.720 --> 00:06:59.200
Well, um...

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:01.650
I was just hoping the demon races 
weren't scaring you.

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:06.370
Oh... Did you find out 
about my fear of demon races?

00:07:06.370 --> 00:07:07.120
Yeah.

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:09.370
Kojou-kun told you, didn't he?

00:07:09.370 --> 00:07:11.660
He should really mind his own business.

00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:15.840
I mean... I don't mean 
to discriminate or anything,

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:20.170
but I guess I'm still scared of vampires 
and therianthropes and stuff...

00:07:20.170 --> 00:07:22.320
Oh, magical beasts don't bother me, though!

00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:26.570
It's like how girls with a fear of men 
are okay around male dogs, y'know?

00:07:26.570 --> 00:07:27.810
Oh...

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:33.550
Hey, just a guess, but are you worried 
about Kojou-kun and Asagi-chan?

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:36.500
Huh? Oh, yeah, a little.

00:07:36.500 --> 00:07:40.430
I feel kind of bad having fun 
while they're stuck working.

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:42.160
That's what bothers you?

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:44.450
Well, we're still in middle school,

00:07:44.450 --> 00:07:46.420
so it's not our fault we can't help.

00:07:46.420 --> 00:07:48.190
Also, that's not what I meant!

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:51.420
Yukina-chan, what do you 
think about Asagi-chan?

00:07:51.420 --> 00:07:54.830
Um... I think she's really cool.

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:57.420
She's brave, kind...

00:07:58.630 --> 00:08:00.990
I love you, Yukina-chan!

00:08:00.990 --> 00:08:02.890
I knew you'd get it!

00:08:02.890 --> 00:08:04.020
That's exactly right!

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:08.000
Asagi-chan is smart, kind, and cool.

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:11.890
It'd be so nice if she were 
actually my big sister.

00:08:11.890 --> 00:08:14.010
She's way too good for Kojou-kun, though.

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:16.520
Um, that's...

00:08:16.780 --> 00:08:20.000
But I feel the same way about you, too!

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:21.080
Pardon?

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:23.360
Of course I like Asagi-chan,

00:08:23.360 --> 00:08:25.540
but I'm neutral in all of this!

00:08:25.540 --> 00:08:28.650
So you can bet I'm rooting for you, too!

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:32.500
U-Um, I think you're mistaken 
about several things.

00:08:32.500 --> 00:08:34.400
I'm not... I mean...

00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:38.630
I'm not sure I could call 
you my big sister, though.

00:08:38.630 --> 00:08:40.450
You can be kind of ditzy.

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:42.460
D-Ditzy?!

00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:44.990
What's happening?

00:08:44.990 --> 00:08:47.210
What was that?

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:49.440
Huh?

00:08:50.650 --> 00:08:52.470
<i>No one else felt it.</i>

00:08:52.680 --> 00:08:55.840
<i>Does that mean it was a wave of magic?</i>

00:08:55.840 --> 00:08:57.500
<i>Surely Senpai didn't...</i>

00:08:57.500 --> 00:09:00.770
<i>But that wasn't the same 
kind of magic as Senpai's,</i>

00:09:01.460 --> 00:09:03.760
<i>and it seemed to come from farther away...</i>

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:12.200
<i>Still, a magic wave so strong 
that we could feel it from so far away?</i>

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:13.290
<i>Who could...</i>

00:09:13.890 --> 00:09:16.370
Yukina-chan! The magical beasts!

00:09:18.420 --> 00:09:20.250
<i>It's because of that wave!</i>

00:09:24.460 --> 00:09:27.350
<i>This isn't good. If they all panic...</i>

00:09:28.010 --> 00:09:29.340
Be still.

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:40.330
Who are you?

00:09:43.480 --> 00:09:45.190
Whoa!

00:09:48.280 --> 00:09:51.140
Huh? What was I just...

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:55.280
It appears the magical 
beasts have calmed down.

00:10:01.310 --> 00:10:02.400
Am I wrong?

00:10:02.710 --> 00:10:05.120
No... you're right.

00:10:05.310 --> 00:10:07.730
That was rather scary, wasn't it?

00:10:07.730 --> 00:10:09.630
Um, who are—

00:10:09.630 --> 00:10:10.600
May I...

00:10:12.760 --> 00:10:14.080
take a picture of you?

00:10:14.400 --> 00:10:17.590
Um, no, I'm... well...

00:10:17.890 --> 00:10:19.500
I'm here on my private time.

00:10:20.270 --> 00:10:22.000
I see. What a shame.

00:10:23.270 --> 00:10:25.480
We will meet again, I'm sure.

00:10:25.900 --> 00:10:30.610
When we do, I hope we can be friends.

00:10:36.050 --> 00:10:38.740
She was pretty, huh?

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:40.260
I wonder if she's older.

00:10:40.830 --> 00:10:43.840
She reminded me of you, a little.

00:10:45.840 --> 00:10:48.710
Hello! I'm from Radaman Kitchen.

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:50.910
I'm here to deliver your drinks.

00:10:51.080 --> 00:10:53.920
Hey, over here. We've been waiting for you.

00:10:54.780 --> 00:10:57.130
We hope to hear from you again soon.

00:10:59.140 --> 00:11:01.760
No one told me it was this far away.

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:03.520
I'll take a break when I'm done...

00:11:03.520 --> 00:11:05.940
But by the time I get back, 
I won't even have time!

00:11:26.480 --> 00:11:28.400
Thank you for your help.

00:11:28.400 --> 00:11:30.860
I've found my friend, so I'll be fine now.

00:11:30.860 --> 00:11:32.730
<i>Sounds like a responsible kid...</i>

00:11:31.370 --> 00:11:32.720
I appreciate everything.

00:11:32.720 --> 00:11:34.410
Oh, crap!

00:11:38.100 --> 00:11:39.040
You're late!

00:11:39.240 --> 00:11:40.850
I'm sorry, okay?

00:11:40.850 --> 00:11:43.550
I couldn't help it. 
The place was really far away.

00:11:44.290 --> 00:11:46.890
And who's this girl?

00:11:46.890 --> 00:11:49.560
You didn't try to hit on her, did you?

00:11:49.940 --> 00:11:51.760
Huh? Hit on who?

00:11:53.960 --> 00:11:57.990
Hey, aren't you the lost child I saw 
at the lifeguard center?

00:11:59.470 --> 00:12:01.580
My name is Eguchi. Eguchi Yume.

00:12:02.300 --> 00:12:03.440
Yume?

00:12:03.560 --> 00:12:04.760
Yes.

00:12:04.760 --> 00:12:08.330
I know it sounds like 
a silly, childish name.

00:12:08.330 --> 00:12:09.840
I'm sorry.

00:12:09.840 --> 00:12:12.840
Does it? It sounds like a normal name to me.

00:12:12.840 --> 00:12:14.080
It's cute.

00:12:14.970 --> 00:12:17.440
R-Really?

00:12:17.440 --> 00:12:19.330
I'm glad, even if you didn't mean it.

00:12:19.770 --> 00:12:22.270
Why are you coming on to her?!

00:12:22.270 --> 00:12:24.100
She's just a little kid!

00:12:25.080 --> 00:12:26.850
Who the hell is coming on to anyone?!

00:12:28.270 --> 00:12:30.300
Yume-chan, right?

00:12:30.300 --> 00:12:32.690
Did you have business 
with someone who works here?

00:12:32.690 --> 00:12:34.900
It's you that I have business with.

00:12:35.360 --> 00:12:37.780
You are Akatsuki Kojou-san, correct?

00:12:37.780 --> 00:12:39.920
How did you know my name?

00:12:39.920 --> 00:12:41.700
We've never met before, have we?

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:45.570
Your girlfriend told me about you.

00:12:45.570 --> 00:12:48.200
She said to come to you 
if I had any trouble.

00:12:48.380 --> 00:12:49.860
G-Girlfriend?!

00:12:49.860 --> 00:12:53.450
I-I have no idea who she means! 
Not so much as a clue!

00:12:53.450 --> 00:12:54.920
Um...

00:12:54.920 --> 00:12:58.310
I know it's none of my business, 
but I don't think cheating is good.

00:12:58.750 --> 00:13:00.550
I'm not cheating on anyone!

00:13:00.550 --> 00:13:03.680
Who the hell even gave you 
that ridiculous idea?

00:13:03.680 --> 00:13:06.400
A tall, pretty lady.

00:13:06.400 --> 00:13:09.760
She has big breasts, 
and she wears her hair like this.

00:13:10.080 --> 00:13:11.350
Wait, you mean...

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:12.710
Kirasaka-san?

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:16.770
Hang on. You saw Kirasaka? 
Is she here at Blue Ely?

00:13:17.290 --> 00:13:19.120
How do you know her?

00:13:19.570 --> 00:13:24.960
She... saved me when I was imprisoned.

00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:26.770
Imprisoned?

00:13:31.630 --> 00:13:33.250
Don't worry.

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:36.190
I promise I'll get you out of here.

00:13:36.190 --> 00:13:37.950
Onee-san...

00:13:39.970 --> 00:13:42.710
I'm a War Dancer 
of the Lion King Organization.

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:46.330
To put it simply, I'm basically 
a magical girl heroine.

00:13:46.560 --> 00:13:48.070
Magical?

00:13:48.070 --> 00:13:50.300
I would have guessed your attribute 
was more... physical.

00:13:50.530 --> 00:13:53.150
And... are you young enough 
to be a magical girl?

00:13:53.150 --> 00:13:56.320
Wait, is that exasperation I hear?

00:13:56.320 --> 00:13:57.280
Here they come!

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:01.210
Okay, just watch.

00:14:01.410 --> 00:14:02.450
Koukarin!

00:14:18.780 --> 00:14:20.210
Wow...

00:14:20.210 --> 00:14:23.010
I told you, I'm a magical girl.

00:14:28.840 --> 00:14:31.410
Hey, can you make it on your own from here?

00:14:31.410 --> 00:14:32.160
What?

00:14:32.160 --> 00:14:34.090
I'll be right behind you. Don't worry.

00:14:34.900 --> 00:14:38.320
But just in case we 
aren't able to join up again,

00:14:38.320 --> 00:14:40.220
go see this guy.

00:14:40.850 --> 00:14:42.400
Akatsuki Kojou
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hSaikai Academy High School
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hClass 1-B

00:14:41.170 --> 00:14:44.300
Akatsuki Kojou-san?

00:14:45.040 --> 00:14:47.190
Is he your boyfriend?

00:14:47.190 --> 00:14:48.250
Bo—

00:14:48.250 --> 00:14:51.440
N-No, he's not! We're not like that yet—

00:14:51.440 --> 00:14:52.020
"Yet"?

00:14:52.880 --> 00:14:54.860
Th-That's not what I meant.

00:14:54.860 --> 00:14:58.290
He's sort of just an extra... I mean, um...

00:15:04.780 --> 00:15:08.100
This little one will lead you 
to somewhere safe.

00:15:08.100 --> 00:15:09.390
Go! Quickly!

00:15:10.250 --> 00:15:11.430
Okay!

00:15:11.640 --> 00:15:15.120
The people chasing us found 
us as we were running away,

00:15:15.120 --> 00:15:17.830
and she told me to go on without her.

00:15:18.710 --> 00:15:21.250
She said she'd be right behind me,

00:15:21.250 --> 00:15:24.610
but I kept waiting and waiting, 
and she didn't come...

00:15:24.610 --> 00:15:26.050
So I...

00:15:27.620 --> 00:15:30.450
Hey, c-come on, don't cry!

00:15:30.450 --> 00:15:32.560
Um... Yume, don't cry!

00:15:32.560 --> 00:15:34.240
I know! Want some yakisoba?

00:15:34.420 --> 00:15:35.760
I've got juice, too!

00:15:35.760 --> 00:15:39.330
Seriously, what the heck are you doing?

00:15:35.760 --> 00:15:39.890
You must be thirsty 
since it's so hot, right?

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:43.340
Good work today. See you both tomorrow.

00:15:43.340 --> 00:15:44.880
Sure.

00:15:43.340 --> 00:15:44.880
Okay.

00:15:46.770 --> 00:15:48.570
We're finally done.

00:15:48.570 --> 00:15:51.200
I'm worn out after all that.

00:15:52.900 --> 00:15:54.350
Nope.

00:15:54.350 --> 00:15:58.900
There's no child named Eguchi Yume 
registered as a resident of Itogami Island.

00:15:58.900 --> 00:16:01.370
Well, Blue Ely is a tourist spot.

00:16:01.870 --> 00:16:05.590
It's possible she's visiting 
from the mainland, I guess.

00:16:05.820 --> 00:16:09.020
What should we do? 
Take her to the police for now?

00:16:09.340 --> 00:16:12.020
No, I'm going to take her to Himeragi first.

00:16:12.610 --> 00:16:15.030
Himeragi-san? Why?

00:16:15.200 --> 00:16:18.880
Well, you know... 
She says Kirasaka saved her,

00:16:18.880 --> 00:16:20.910
and Kirasaka is Himeragi's friend, right?

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:23.990
So I figured she might 
know something... maybe...

00:16:25.880 --> 00:16:28.770
Besides, look at her. She's out cold.

00:16:28.770 --> 00:16:30.720
Let's just take her back 
to the cottage for now,

00:16:30.720 --> 00:16:33.460
and we can think about what 
to do with her later.

00:16:33.460 --> 00:16:36.170
Yaze did say there was an extra bed.

00:16:36.690 --> 00:16:37.890
Okay, fine.

00:16:39.330 --> 00:16:41.150
Oh, I forgot. Hold up, Kojou.

00:16:41.530 --> 00:16:43.080
Do you have any money on you?

00:16:43.080 --> 00:16:45.400
Yeah, some... but why?

00:16:45.670 --> 00:16:49.990
We can't make Yume-chan wander 
around in her swimsuit forever.

00:16:50.200 --> 00:16:53.110
Oh, good point...

00:16:53.110 --> 00:16:54.740
Wait, I have to pay for it?!

00:16:54.740 --> 00:16:57.720
Maybe I'm imagining it, 
but this store looks crazy expensive!

00:16:57.910 --> 00:16:59.780
It's the Aldeigia royal 
family's preferred brand,

00:16:59.780 --> 00:17:03.000
and this is the first store 
they've opened in Japan.

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:04.210
Hey!

00:17:06.430 --> 00:17:07.170
What?

00:17:07.340 --> 00:17:08.840
Sayaka-san?

00:17:08.840 --> 00:17:11.700
Yeah. Seems she's here at Blue Ely.

00:17:11.700 --> 00:17:13.260
Any idea where she might be?

00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:16.150
I see.

00:17:17.650 --> 00:17:20.720
Let's ride one more time, Yukina-chan...

00:17:20.720 --> 00:17:22.880
In any case, is it all right 
if I see this girl

00:17:22.880 --> 00:17:25.590
who says Sayaka-san saved her?

00:17:25.590 --> 00:17:26.640
Sure.

00:17:28.620 --> 00:17:31.040
She might still be asleep, though.

00:17:31.350 --> 00:17:32.940
Coming in, Asagi.

00:17:36.520 --> 00:17:38.450
Er... huh?

00:17:38.750 --> 00:17:40.880
Don't you "huh?" me!

00:17:40.880 --> 00:17:43.590
Why the hell would you walk
into a girl's room without knocking?!

00:17:43.590 --> 00:17:44.580
You jerk!

00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:51.440
Senpai...

00:17:52.100 --> 00:17:55.560
Woohoo! Meat, baby!

00:17:55.560 --> 00:17:57.040
You eating, Kojou?

00:17:57.040 --> 00:18:00.610
This is some gorgeous 
top-grade meat I brought ya!

00:18:00.610 --> 00:18:02.840
What's top-grade about this?

00:18:02.840 --> 00:18:04.880
Also, you should be helping me cook

00:18:04.430 --> 00:18:06.770
<b>Half Off</b>

00:18:04.880 --> 00:18:06.540
this half-off sale meat.

00:18:09.040 --> 00:18:10.510
I mean, it's good, though.

00:18:10.970 --> 00:18:13.840
Hey, Asagi, we've got some more ready.

00:18:16.190 --> 00:18:18.250
I said it was an accident...

00:18:18.250 --> 00:18:21.300
Okay, mine's all grilled up, too!

00:18:21.300 --> 00:18:23.530
Here, Kojou-kun and Yazecchi!

00:18:23.760 --> 00:18:26.290
Nagisa?! You... What...

00:18:27.760 --> 00:18:30.660
I ended up not going to the pool today,

00:18:30.660 --> 00:18:33.020
so I thought I could at least wear it now.

00:18:33.160 --> 00:18:36.480
Whoa! Lookin' pretty nice, Nagisa-chan!

00:18:36.480 --> 00:18:39.050
You know exactly what 
sparks a guy's interest!

00:18:39.050 --> 00:18:41.780
I asked Yukina-chan to wear hers with me,

00:18:41.780 --> 00:18:44.400
but she was too embarrassed to do it.

00:18:44.400 --> 00:18:46.270
Disappointed, aren't you, Kojou-kun?

00:18:46.620 --> 00:18:48.870
I'm not disappointed.

00:18:48.870 --> 00:18:50.610
Anyway, forget about that.

00:18:50.610 --> 00:18:53.070
You seemed like you weren't 
feeling well when you got back.

00:18:53.070 --> 00:18:54.530
Are you okay now?

00:18:54.800 --> 00:18:57.920
That was just from taking 
too many roller coaster rides.

00:18:57.920 --> 00:19:00.560
Anyway, Kojou-kun, behind you...

00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:05.920
You're not disappointed, you say?

00:19:05.920 --> 00:19:08.180
"Forget about that," you say?

00:19:08.180 --> 00:19:09.510
I see.

00:19:09.720 --> 00:19:11.710
Um... Himeragi?

00:19:11.990 --> 00:19:14.350
No, nothing's wrong at all.

00:19:14.780 --> 00:19:17.520
Thank you for letting me 
use your cell phone.

00:19:17.540 --> 00:19:18.930
S-Sure...

00:19:19.470 --> 00:19:21.310
So, how'd it go?

00:19:21.310 --> 00:19:24.890
As I expected, I couldn't get 
any answers about her mission.

00:19:25.110 --> 00:19:27.400
But the teacher did tell me

00:19:27.400 --> 00:19:30.850
that no other War Dancer has been sent 
to take Sayaka-san's place.

00:19:31.390 --> 00:19:33.440
Teacher?

00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:36.080
Oh, you mean Cat-sensei?

00:19:36.910 --> 00:19:40.790
So does that mean Kirasaka 
is still working on her mission?

00:19:41.140 --> 00:19:44.460
Well, it's safe to say 
she's still alive, at least.

00:19:44.610 --> 00:19:48.370
Then why didn't she come 
to get Yume herself?

00:19:48.620 --> 00:19:49.610
Um...

00:19:50.650 --> 00:19:55.150
It may be that she's trying to meet Riru.

00:19:55.730 --> 00:19:57.670
Riru? Who's that?

00:19:58.280 --> 00:19:59.470
My older sister.

00:19:59.470 --> 00:20:04.610
She was imprisoned in the 
Kusuki Elysee laboratory with me.

00:20:04.960 --> 00:20:08.240
Kusuki Elysee... I've heard 
that name somewhere before.

00:20:08.570 --> 00:20:11.020
They're sponsoring Blue Elysium.

00:20:11.310 --> 00:20:14.610
They're mainly in charge 
of running the magical beast park.

00:20:14.700 --> 00:20:16.760
Why would a company like theirs do that?

00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:24.600
Hey, Yume, what was Kusuki Elysee 
holding you two prisoner for?

00:20:25.120 --> 00:20:28.620
Oh, of course, you don't have to 
tell me if you don't want to.

00:20:28.800 --> 00:20:33.320
But if your sister's still there, 
she might be in danger, right?

00:20:33.980 --> 00:20:37.580
I don't think you need to worry about Riru.

00:20:38.230 --> 00:20:43.560
It was Riru that the people 
at Kusuki Elysee needed, not me.

00:20:43.560 --> 00:20:47.600
She willingly cooperated 
in their experiments from the start.

00:20:47.860 --> 00:20:48.880
Experiments?

00:20:49.320 --> 00:20:52.480
I... don't want to talk 
about that right now.

00:20:52.660 --> 00:20:53.920
I'm sorry.

00:20:54.560 --> 00:20:56.130
I see...

00:20:56.130 --> 00:20:59.640
No, I'm sorry. I said you didn't 
have to talk if you didn't want to.

00:21:01.280 --> 00:21:05.560
Man, I'm not used to talking about serious 
stuff like this! It's making me hungry!

00:21:06.300 --> 00:21:08.630
I'm gonna go chow down!

00:21:09.880 --> 00:21:12.900
Wait, what? Where's the meat?!

00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:15.010
We had enough to feed twelve!

00:21:18.700 --> 00:21:20.160
You're kidding me!

00:21:20.490 --> 00:21:22.060
Don't tell me... you ate it all...

00:21:25.210 --> 00:21:27.100
No way!

00:21:47.290 --> 00:21:49.410
How's the serpent doing?

00:21:49.860 --> 00:21:53.800
It is still traveling 
southeast along the ley line.

00:21:54.600 --> 00:21:57.390
It should pass through 
the vicinity of Itogami Island

00:21:57.390 --> 00:22:00.020
between tomorrow afternoon 
and early morning the next day.

00:22:00.260 --> 00:22:03.420
Good. All is basically 
proceeding as planned.

00:22:04.170 --> 00:22:07.010
And the girl's vessel still hasn't returned?

00:22:07.310 --> 00:22:09.710
There it no need to worry.

00:22:09.710 --> 00:22:12.140
She will come back, without question...

00:22:12.140 --> 00:22:13.550
and willingly.

00:22:13.650 --> 00:22:15.050
I have my concerns,

00:22:15.520 --> 00:22:17.920
but if you say so, I'll trust you.

00:22:17.920 --> 00:22:20.730
You have been such a great help, after all.

00:22:21.170 --> 00:22:22.930
You honor me,

00:22:22.930 --> 00:22:24.240
Chairman Kusuki.

00:22:24.550 --> 00:22:26.640
I except nothing but the best.

00:22:38.410 --> 00:22:40.120
Have you awakened?

00:22:40.120 --> 00:22:41.840
I let my guard down.

00:22:41.840 --> 00:22:44.940
If I had known you could 
use a technique like that,

00:22:44.940 --> 00:22:47.330
I could have found a way to deal with it...

00:22:49.660 --> 00:22:52.540
You think an elementary school 
girl can escape here alone?

00:22:52.800 --> 00:22:54.320
She's not alone.

00:22:54.320 --> 00:22:56.390
I'm going to be right behind her!

00:22:56.560 --> 00:22:59.860
A Der Freischütz from 
the Lion King Organization...

00:22:59.860 --> 00:23:02.690
A prototype suppression weapon engraved with

00:23:02.690 --> 00:23:04.940
a spell for severing spatial connections.

00:23:05.930 --> 00:23:08.730
It is certainly a powerful weapon...

00:23:10.910 --> 00:23:13.750
But at this range, you can't 
use its unique type-six attacks.

00:23:13.920 --> 00:23:17.540
War Dancer weapons are specialized 
for hexes and assassination.

00:23:18.330 --> 00:23:21.330
You aren't suited for fighting alone 
at close range, are you?

00:23:21.650 --> 00:23:22.760
Am I wrong?

00:23:22.870 --> 00:23:24.890
That's not always the case!

00:23:25.380 --> 00:23:26.270
Restrict!

00:23:29.270 --> 00:23:30.510
Blazing Thunder!

00:23:39.430 --> 00:23:40.760
Rending Thunder!

00:23:46.640 --> 00:23:49.530
Blazing Thunder and Rending Thunder...

00:23:50.490 --> 00:23:54.040
Are you also... a Sword Shaman?

00:23:54.670 --> 00:23:56.480
I am the Six-Blade Priestess...

00:23:57.450 --> 00:23:59.240
The Sword Shaman of Shadow.
